from [Stacks, Tag 099F] at a sheaf of ideals of finite type"]
theorem isDerivedComplete_derivedPushforward_derivedCompletion_inverseImageIdealSheaf
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))) :
    IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} Y (generatedIdealSheaf t)
      ((derivedPushforward.{u} f.toRingedToposSiteHom).obj
        ((derivedCompletion X (generatedIdealSheaf (pushGlobalSections f hT' t))).obj K)) :=
  isDerivedComplete_derivedPushforward_derivedCompletion_generatedIdealSheaf f _ t
    (pushforwardIdealCompatible_pushGlobalSections f hT hT' t) K

include hT in
/-- **The canonical comparison map `(Rf_*K)^∧ ⟶ Rf_*(K^∧)` of [Stacks, Tag 0A0G] at the source's
own ideal sheaves.** It exists because `Rf_*(K^∧)` is derived complete, by [Stacks, Tag 099J];
it is built as a mate and is therefore natural in `K`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionPushforwardComparisonGeneratedIdealSheaf`
at `ℐ = (t_1, …, t_s)` and `ℐ' = f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X`. It is invertible at every object of `D(𝒪')`,
which is the tag's assertion:
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_inverseImageIdealSheaf`
of `PushforwardCommutesCompletionCanonical.lean`, and
`isIso_natTrans_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_inverseImageIdealSheaf` there for the
whole natural transformation. -/
@[stacks 0A0G "the canonical comparison map `(Rf_*K)^∧ ⟶ Rf_*(K^∧)` that the tag asserts to be \
invertible, at a morphism of ringed sites sending a terminal object of the target site to a \
terminal object of the source site, with `ℐ` generated by finitely many global sections of `𝒪` \
and the completion on the source taken along `f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X` — the ideal sheaf Section 52.7 \
builds out of `ℐ`, which here is constructed from `f` and the generators of `ℐ` and identified \
as that ideal sheaf by \
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.eq_generatedIdealSheaf_pushGlobalSections`. Both derived \
completion functors are produced from the generators, by \
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf`. This map \
is invertible at every object of `D(𝒪')`, which is the tag's assertion, by \
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_inverseImageIdealSheaf` \
of `PushforwardCommutesCompletionCanonical.lean`. At the tag's own `ℐ`, which is of finite type \
and hence only *locally* generated by finitely many sections, the derived completion functors \
come instead from [Stacks, Tag 099F] at a sheaf of ideals of finite type, \
